quran[29]{c,v,t}:
  70,11,"(although) they will be made to see each other. The guilty will wish to ransom himself from the punishment of that Day at the expense of his children,"
  70,12,"and his wife and his brother,"
  70,13,"and his close family who had sheltered him,"
  70,14,"and all those upon the earth, if it could save him (from the punishment)."
  70,15,"But never! Indeed, it is a blazing Fire,"
  70,16,that strips away the whole skin.
  70,17,"It invites whoever turns back and flees (from the truth),"
  70,18,and accumulates wealth and holds it (from distribution).
  70,19,"Indeed, humankind has been created impatient and greedy."
  70,20,"He gets distressed when misfortune afflicts him,"
  70,21,"and he becomes miserly when good fortune comes his way,"
  70,22,"except for the performers of prayer,"
  70,23,"those who consistently observe their prayers,"
  70,24,"and those in whose wealth there is a known share,"
  70,25,"for the beggar and the deprived,"
  70,26,"and those who firmly believe in the Day of Judgement,"
  70,27,and those who are fearful of the punishment of their Lord.
  70,28,"Indeed, the punishment of their Lord is not something to feel safe from."
  70,29,"And those who guard (the chastity of) their private parts,"
  70,30,"except with their wives or their slave women, for they are not blameworthy (for them)."
  70,31,But those who seek to go beyond this (limit) are the transgressors.
  70,32,"And those who are faithful in keeping their trusts and covenants,"
  70,33,"and those who are firm upholders of their testimonies,"
  70,34,"and those who are (consistently) watchful over their prayers,"
  70,35,"they shall be in Gardens, held in great honour."
  70,36,"What is the matter with the disbelievers that they are hastening towards you,"
  70,37,"from the right and the left, in crowds (to mock you)?"
  70,38,Does every one of them hope to enter the Garden of Bliss (without possessing faith and performing good deeds)?
  70,39,"Never! Indeed, We have created them from (a substance) they already know."
